# .gitignore for an Ignition 8.3 repository rooted at the Gateway data/ folder
# (the "full data directory" layout).
#
# Source: Inductive Automation, "Version and Source Control Guide", Ignition 8.3 manual
#   https://www.docs.inductiveautomation.com/docs/8.3/tutorials/version-control-guide
# The patterns below are IA's recommended list from that guide. Re-check the guide
# when you upgrade Ignition; the list may change.
#
# Optional: binary (.bin) resources.
#   IA recommends also ignoring Transaction Groups, Client Tags, Reports and
#   Alarm Pipelines, which are stored as Java .bin files. The guide names the
#   resource types but not their folders. Find their folders in your own data/
#   tree and add those paths below if you choose to ignore them. Changes to
#   Alarm Pipelines need human engineering review whether or not they are tracked.
#
# For the curated-mount (container) layout, IA's shorter list is:
#   **/config/local
#   **/config/resources/local
#   **/conversion-report.txt
#   **/.resources/
# plus, when core is committed (tested on 8.3.9; see docker.md rule 4), these
# per-Gateway resources that every Gateway creates on first boot:
#   **/config/resources/core/ignition/user-source/
#   **/config/resources/core/ignition/identity-provider/temp/
#   **/config/resources/core/ignition/opc-connection/
#   **/config/resources/core/ignition/system-properties/
#   **/config/resources/core/ignition/gateway-network-queue-settings/
#   **/config/resources/core/ignition/gateway-network-proxy-rules/
#   **/config/resources/core/ignition/quickstart/
#   **/config/resources/core/com.inductiveautomation.opcua/one-time/
#   **/migration-log-*.md

# Database files
**/db/
**/metricsdb/
**/autobackup/
**/db_backup_sqlite.idb
**/valueStore.idb

# Cache and temporary files
**/jar-cache/
**/request
**/response
*.tmp
*.bak
**/var

# Log files
*.log
**/logs

# Certificates and security
**/certificates/
**/keystore/

# Runtime configuration (environment-specific)
**/config/local
**/config/resources/local

# Gateway-specific runtime files
**/.container-init.conf

# Backup and converted files
**/conversion-report.txt
**.digest.json

# Project conversion artifacts
**/projects/conversion-report.txt
**/migration-log-*.md
**/.resources/

# Alarm history files
**/.alarms_*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Additions by this project (not in IA's list)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets Management key files (root.json, kek.json). IA's list does not cover
# this path; if these leak, every embedded secret in the repo can be decrypted.
**/config/ignition/keys/
#
# Tested against a live 8.3.9 Gateway data/ folder: with IA's list, git still
# tracked these credential-bearing files. Decide per repo whether to ignore them:
#   config/resources/*/ignition/user-source/*/users.json    internal users with password hashes
#   config/resources/*/ignition/api-token/*/config.json     API key hashes
#   any resource config.json with an embedded secret        (JWE: "ciphertext", "encrypted_key")
# Prefer Referenced secrets from a secret provider for anything committed to git.
